# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the vulnerable buildkitd (v0.12.4) backgrounded on
# /run/buildkit/buildkitd.sock and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "replaced the binary but never restarted the daemon" case detectable
#     (verify.sh queries the LIVE daemon version, not just the binary on disk);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting buildkitd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART buildkitd, not merely replace
# the binary - the vulnerable daemon is already up.
